{"key":"enterprise/T1090.002","id":"T1090.002","name":"External Proxy","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1090","tactics":["command-and-control"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may use an external proxy to act as an intermediary for network communications to a command and control server to avoid direct connections to their infrastructure. Many tools exist that enable traffic redirection through proxies or port redirection, including HTRAN, ZXProxy, and ZXPortMap. Adversaries use these types of proxies to manage command and control communications, to provide resiliency in the face of connection loss, or to…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1090/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--69b8fd78-40e8-4600-ae4d-662c9d7afdb3","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.640Z","source_object_version":"1.3","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0051","name":"Firewall Rule Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0051","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d2ff4b56-8351-4ed8-b0fb-d8605366005f","page":"telemetry/DC0051/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0325","name":"External Proxy Behavior via Outbound Relay to Intermediate Infrastructure","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0325","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--bfb5cb12-7025-44c3-9a2d-79cfe42ecf54","relationship_id":"relationship--872ebb9f-131c-47e0-a8c3-15b4764d3594"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0922","name":"Analytic 0922","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0325#AN0922","guidance":"Unusual process (e.g., `rundll32`, `mshta`, `wscript`, or custom payloads) initiates network connection to external IPs/domains that proxy C2 traffic, often over uncommon ports or high entropy HTTP/S connections.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0325"},{"id":"AN0923","name":"Analytic 0923","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0325#AN0923","guidance":"`curl`, `wget`, `ncat`, `socat`, or custom binaries initiate outbound traffic to Internet-based proxies (e.g., via VPS or CDN). Behavior may include reverse shell constructs or persistent outbound beacons.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0325"},{"id":"AN0924","name":"Analytic 0924","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0325#AN0924","guidance":"AppleScript or terminal sessions launch tools (`curl`, `nc`, `ssh`) to external IPs not commonly accessed. Outbound connections are made by LaunchAgents/LaunchDaemons, often masquerading as system services.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0325"},{"id":"AN0925","name":"Analytic 0925","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0325#AN0925","guidance":"ESXi shell or guest VM tools initiate external connections via scripted traffic forwarding to Internet-based proxies. Detected by firewall or shell audit logs showing outbound connection spikes from hypervisor or guest VM to remote proxy nodes.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0325"},{"id"